{#- Dessert fridge sign (client 2026-10-29): black & white, no logo, the
    desserts one to a line with their price. They're read from Square
    (src/_data/desserts.json, made by scripts/desserts.js: the kitchen
    board's Manage -> Desserts), so when the desserts change, change them
    there, `npm run build` (or `npm run desserts`), commit desserts.json
    and print a new sheet. A kind Square counts at 0 is left off.
    `skipDesserts` above leaves whole items off: the bars have their own
    sign (sign-dessert-bars-bw.njk), and Cheesecake is off while the cafe
    is out of it (client 2026-10-29: only Plain is counted in Square, so
    the count alone wouldn't drop it). If you find yourself typing a
    dessert or a price here, stop. -#}
<div class="canvas sign sign--bw fd">
    <div class="sign-heading">
        <h2 class="p-display sign-heading-title">Desserts</h2>
    </div>

    <ul class="sign-rows fd-rows">
        {%- for item in desserts.items %}
        {%- if item.name not in skipDesserts %}
        {%- set kinds = item.kinds | rejectattr("out") %}
        {%- for k in kinds %}
        <li class="sign-row">
            <div class="sign-row-head">
                <span class="sign-row-name">{{ k.name }}</span>
                <span class="sign-row-fill" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                <span class="sign-row-price">{{ item.price | money }}</span>
            </div>
            {%- if loop.last %}
            {%- for l in item.lists %}
            <p class="sign-row-sub">{{ l.name }}: {{ l.options | join(" or ") }}</p>
            {%- endfor %}
            {%- endif %}
        </li>
        {%- endfor %}
        {%- endif %}
        {%- endfor %}
    </ul>
</div>
